  "description": "A single spacecraft in a circular low-Earth orbit around a point-mass Earth: no perturbations and no attitude. The \"hello world\" of orbital mechanics. (The inclination is a Sun-synchronous one, but without Earth's oblateness the orbit plane does not actually turn to follow the Sun.)\n\nWhat to look at:\n- sat-1.position_N traces a perfect circle.\n- The period matches Kepler's third law: about 92.6 minutes, so one day is ~15.5 orbits.\n\nTry changing:\n- Semi-major axis: higher means a slower orbit and a longer period.\n- Inclination: watch the ground track change in Vizard.\n- Eccentricity: see template 02 for an elliptical orbit.",
